# 2.3) Build with Genie Code

On this page, you will use **Genie Code** to create dashboard widgets with a single natural-language prompt on the `② Build with Genie Code` tab.

## Task 1 - Open Genie Code

1. Click the `② Build with Genie Code` tab at the top.

    {{ shot('02-aibi-dashboard/2-3-01-page-2.png', '② Build with Genie Code tab') }}

2. Click the **Genie Code** icon in the top right. The Genie Code panel opens on the right with an input field at the bottom.

    {{ shot('02-aibi-dashboard/2-3-02-open-genie-code.png', 'Open Genie Code panel') }}

## Task 2 - Enter a prompt

1. Paste the prompt below into the Genie Code input field and submit.

    !!! prompt "Prompt"
        ```text
        {{ g.prompt | trim | indent(8) }}
        ```

    !!! tip "Why include definitions in the prompt?"
        {{ g.prompt_tip | trim | indent(8) }}

    {{ shot('02-aibi-dashboard/2-3-03-prompt.png', 'Enter prompt') }}

2. Genie Code reads the dashboard configuration and data, then creates widgets and places them on the canvas. The step names shown in the panel may vary. This takes about a minute. Wait until a summary appears in the panel.

    {{ shot('02-aibi-dashboard/2-3-04-generating.png', 'Genie Code creating widgets') }}

## Task 3 - Review results and refine

1. Check the widgets Genie Code created. Verify that all requested items appear:

    | Item | Widget type (example) |
    |---|---|
{% for r in g.expected %}
    | {{ r.item }} | {{ r.widget }} |
{% endfor %}

    {{ shot('02-aibi-dashboard/2-3-05-result.png', 'Widgets created by Genie Code') }}

2. Widgets created by Genie Code are automatically applied to the canvas. If any widget has an error (**Unable to render visualization**) or needs adjusting, enter a follow-up request in the same panel. {{ g.followup_intro }}

    !!! prompt "Prompt"
        ```text
        {{ g.followup_prompt | trim | indent(8) }}
        ```

    {{ shot('02-aibi-dashboard/2-3-06-accept.png', 'Update a widget with a follow-up request') }}

!!! tip "Results may vary slightly"
    Since Genie Code is a generative AI, the same prompt can produce slightly different widget types, layouts, and titles for each user. If the result doesn't match expectations, refine with follow-up requests like "{{ g.refine_example }}"

## Task 4 - Publish the dashboard

1. Click **Publish** in the top right.

    {{ shot('02-aibi-dashboard/2-3-07-publish.png', 'Publish') }}

2. Keep the **Share data permission** option at default and click **Publish**. After the sharing settings window appears, close it and click **View published** at the top to see the published dashboard. The published version shows only the two page tabs without the **Data** tab.

    {{ shot('02-aibi-dashboard/2-3-08-published.png', 'Published dashboard') }}

!!! success "Congratulations!"
    You have completed the {{ s.dashboard.title }} dashboard. However, metrics like {{ g.local_metrics }} are defined only in this dashboard's SQL, so if someone calculates them elsewhere, the numbers might differ. In the next Step, {{ da.name }} will define business metrics using **Unity Catalog Semantics** so the whole organization sees the same numbers.
